{#
_contacts_pane.html.twig — the address book docked beside the mail panes.

The container, the handle and the sizing are _side_pane.html.twig's, shared
with the calendar. Two things differ, and both because the calendar was there
first and owns the shell:

  - Its ui--split is on this wrapper, not the shell. A boundary is one
    controller, the shell's is the calendar's, and Stimulus gives a target to
    the NEAREST controller of its name, so the handle and pane below are this
    one's. It cannot see the mail pane as a target for the same reason, and
    measures it by selector instead (main-selector).
  - Its positions (closed, beside the mail, full width) are not ui--split's
    but contacts--pane's, on the shell, which also decides when it and the
    calendar can be docked side by side. The boundary only snaps: dragged
    past either end it reports `snap`, and contacts--pane makes that full
    width or closed, as the calendar's handle does for the calendar. Anywhere
    but beside the mail the boundary is `data-split-held` and leaves the
    width alone (ui--split's _reclamp()), from the first paint on.

The pane runs the whole address book. Every contacts page renders into
`contacts-pane-frame` when the frame asks for it — see contacts/_layout.html.twig
— so a list, a contact, the editor and the merge all stay in the pane, and the
mail beside it never reloads.
#}

{# The full contacts page hands over its own page as `contactsPaneBody` (see
   contacts/_page_shell.html.twig): open, whatever is remembered, and with no
   list rendered only to be replaced. #}
{% set paneOpen = contactsPaneBody is defined or app.user.contactsPaneOpen %}

{% embed '_partials/_side_pane.html.twig' with {
    name: 'contacts',
    open: paneOpen,
    widthVar: '--contacts-pane-width',
    width: app.user.contactsPaneWidth,
    handleLabel: 'contacts.pane.resize'|trans,
    controller: 'ui--side-split',
    attrs: 'data-contacts--pane-target="dock"'
        ~ ' data-controller="ui--side-split"'
        ~ ' data-ui--side-split-modes-value="false"'
        ~ ' data-ui--side-split-snap-value="true"'
        ~ (contactsPaneBody is defined or 'split' != app.user.contactsPaneMode.value ? ' data-split-held' : '')
        ~ ' data-action="ui--side-split:snap->contacts--pane#snapped"'
        ~ ' data-ui--side-split-variable-value="--contacts-pane-width"'
        ~ ' data-ui--side-split-main-selector-value="[data-ui--split-target=&quot;main&quot;]"'
        ~ ' data-ui--side-split-state-url-value="' ~ path('app_contacts_pane_state') ~ '"'
        ~ ' data-ui--side-split-token-value="' ~ csrf_token('contacts_pane_state') ~ '"'
        ~ ' data-ui--side-split-min-value="' ~ constant('App\\Entity\\User\\User::CONTACTS_PANE_MIN_WIDTH') ~ '"'
        ~ ' data-ui--side-split-max-value="' ~ constant('App\\Entity\\User\\User::CONTACTS_PANE_MAX_WIDTH') ~ '"'
        ~ ' data-ui--side-split-default-value="' ~ constant('App\\Entity\\User\\User::CONTACTS_PANE_DEFAULT_WIDTH') ~ '"',
} %}
    {% block side_pane_body %}
        {# Rendered with the page when it will be seen on first paint, lazy and
           empty otherwise — the calendar pane's reasoning. The attribute is
           what tells the contacts layout this is the pane, as the frame's
           header does for a navigation inside it. #}
        {% if contactsPaneBody is defined %}
            {{ contactsPaneBody }}
        {% elseif open %}
            {{ render(controller('App\\Controller\\Contacts\\ContactController::list', { _contacts_pane: true })) }}
        {% else %}
            <turbo-frame
                id="contacts-pane-frame"
                loading="lazy"
                class="flex flex-col min-h-0 flex-1"
            >
                <div class="flex items-center justify-center h-24 text-ink-faint" aria-live="polite">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-notch fa-spin" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                </div>
            </turbo-frame>
        {% endif %}
    {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}
